    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d514">

                <pb facs="0858" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/319: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sussdorff</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-24T16:00:00+01:19"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 24—12:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>72. Department’s circular of June 29, 3 p.m.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d514-f1"/>
                    Dutch Government states that before it gives its formal adhesion again to the
                    amended resolution of the United States Government covering shipment of arms and
                    munitions of war to China it desires to learn whether Italian Government has
                    adhered without reservation to the amended resolution.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sussdorff</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
